<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>South of Crete, 1985</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-bidi-font-weight: bold"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;South of Crete 1985&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-bidi-font-weight: bold"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Ships that go bump in the night!&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-bidi-font-weight: bold"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;24 December 1985 22:00:00 UTC /25 December 1985 00:00:01&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Mediterranean Sea, Vicinity of Crete&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Updated&amp;nbsp;to C:MO V1.02 Build 1147.14 on 6 November 2020&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-bidi-font-weight: bold"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Al Sandrik / Beirutdude&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-bidi-font-weight: bold"&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;As the sudden crisis between the United States/NATO and the Soviet Union escalated in the Central and Northern Fronts not much really seemed to be happening in the Mediterranean. Soviet ships came and went into the Fifth Eskadra’s anchorage east of Crete with no change in tempo. That all changed on Christmas Eve, 1985 when monitors noted a five ship flotilla, led by the CG Slava, making its way to the south. USS Yorktown (CG-48) has been detached from the USS Saratoga (CV-60) CVBG (CTF 60.1) and assigned to TF 60.2 to provide additional SAM and EW support. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-bidi-font-weight: bold"&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;NOTES: &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-bidi-font-weight: bold"&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;There is a prewar and war phase of this scenario. The war starts when conflict begins on the Central Front in Germany. You may not begin the war&amp;nbsp;by initiating hostilities (obviously I can’t enforce this). So both sides play a cat and mouse game of detection and evasion prior to the war breaking out sometime about sunrise on&amp;nbsp;December 25th. This may seem boring, but think about how the commanders would be on edge with the tracking of an enemy force and waiting for something to happen, and worse, with the initiation of hostilities in someone else’s hands. So if that isn’t your thing, that’s OK but if you really want to get the most out of the design, and intent I think it will be a bit nail biting. I’ve played it about 20 times with about 15 very different results. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-bidi-font-weight: bold"&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Also due to surface TF teleports and the need to have&amp;nbsp;AI missions teleport with them please run the sceanrio for 2 or so seconds before setting up any missions. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-bidi-font-weight: bold"&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;IMPORTANT: With the restriction above players must &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;I&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold"&gt;ensure that all ASW Missions are Weapons Tight&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/I&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;! Command sets all ASW missions to weapons free for ASW Weapons Control Status (I really don’t get the logic of it, but it does). So please ensure the doctrine of all ASW Missions is set to “Tight” to avoid premature conflict. &lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;I&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-WEIGHT: normal; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold"&gt;In the real world&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/I&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;, the USS Comte de Grasse (DD-974) had just departed the Med on December 5th, 1985, USS Talbot was in the United States &lt;EM&gt;but positioned for combat&lt;/EM&gt;, both USS McInerney (FFG-8) and USS Yorktown (CG-48) were both deployed to the Med during this period. USS Tinosa SSN-606 deployed to the Med in Jan of 1986.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-bidi-font-weight: bold"&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;An INI and DELTA file are both provided for rebuilds.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-bidi-font-weight: bold"&gt;&lt;A&gt;&lt;SPAN style="COLOR: windowtext"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;Al.sandrik@gmail.com&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/A&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P style="TEXT-ALIGN: center" align=center&gt;&lt;FONT color=white&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
